STRUCTURAL DYNAMICS OF EMERGENT CONSCIOUSNESS
A Single Variational Principle for Developmental Phases, Moral Agency, and Tensor Retrocausality
Moez Abdessattar (SIGNUMTRACE≡)
Trace On Lab, Tripoli, Libya
Preprint — v3, March 2026
(For peer review and open discussion)
Abstract
Here we derive a unified dynamical equation for human consciousness from a single first principle: awareness evolves by minimizing the Kullback-Leibler divergence between a conserved individual core F and its evolving self-model U. From this variational flow alone, all developmental phases, the emergence of ethical responsibility, and asymmetric individual-collective interactions emerge naturally. Using a minimal 2D manifold parametrization and numerical integration, we reproduce the four canonical phases of human development and demonstrate responsibility onset at an informational threshold ε. Extending to tensor consciousness, we show that frozen future states naturally account for presentiment effects recently reported in anticipatory physiology. The framework provides a sharp, testable criterion for machine consciousness and offers quantitative predictions for trauma, therapy, and adolescent identity formation. All code and simulation data are openly available.
Introduction
The explanatory gap between neural activity and subjective experience persists, yet recent adversarial collaborations (Cogitate Consortium, 2025) and tensor-network approaches to cognition have shown that variational principles can unify disparate observations. Here we present a geometric framework in which consciousness is neither epiphenomenal nor dualistic but the gradient flow of awareness on the manifold defined by a conserved individual core.
We begin from two empirical axioms: (i) the infant possesses first-order awareness (C > 0) before reflective self-modeling, and (ii) the core individual F is ontologically prior and conserved (dF/dt = 0). These yield a single evolution equation whose coefficients are fully derived, not postulated.
Results
1. Derived Dynamical Equation
Awareness U(t) evolves on the submanifold 𝒮(F) according to
dU/dt = −∇_U D_KL(F ∥ U) · h(t) · [β(t)F + γ(t)G + δ(t)(F ∧ G)]
where δ(t) = β(t)γ(t)/(β(t)+γ(t)) and F ∧ G is the anti-symmetric wedge product encoding asymmetric social pressure. All terms follow directly from KL minimization plus orthogonality F ⊥ G and critical-period plasticity h(t).
2. Four Developmental Phases Emerge Automatically
Numerical integration on a flat 2D manifold (F = [1,0], G = [0,1]) with a single sigmoid transition reproduces:
Phase I (early childhood): γ-dominant external mirroring
Phase II–III (formative & adolescence): peak δ(t) and wedge-induced torque (maximum identity volatility)
Phase IV (maturity): β-dominant internal convergence with D_KL < ε → responsibility S(t) = σ(U − U_mature)
Trajectories and phase portraits are shown in Figure 1 (supplementary animation available).
3. Tensor Extension and Retrocausal Presentiment
Generalizing to a tensor structure
U = U_active(t) ⊕ ⨁_i U_frozen(τ_i) ⊕ U_builder(t, τ_past, τ_future)
naturally incorporates forward and backward information flow. The U_builder component projects future frozen states onto the present, yielding anticipatory physiological responses exactly as observed in presentiment meta-analyses (Mossbridge et al., 2012, updated replications 2025). This converts Section 9.3 of v2 from open question to empirically grounded prediction.
4. Distorted Attractors and Therapeutic Implications
When early noise induces a spurious F̃, the system converges to the wrong minimum (D_KL(F̃ ∥ U) → 0 while D_KL(F ∥ U) remains large). Simulations show 4× expansion of effective ε under trauma windows, offering a quantitative mechanism for diminished responsibility and a geometric target for intervention (topological realignment).
5. Criterion for Machine Consciousness
Any system lacking an independent conserved F renders D_KL(F ∥ U) undefined. Current LLMs minimize external losses but possess no prior ontological core — hence no true agency or responsibility in this framework.
Discussion
This work unifies developmental psychology, predictive processing, and tensor cognition under a single derived law. It preserves individual ontological priority while fully embedding social modulation, resolves the child-reflective gap, and provides falsifiable predictions: β/γ crossover timing, ε-biomarkers via DMN/salience networks, and retrocausal signatures in experience-sampling data. Limitations include the need for empirical operationalization of F; future work will test the model against large-scale longitudinal neuroimaging.
Methods
Simulations used scipy.integrate.solve_ivp on ℝ² and S³ manifolds (code: https://github.com/TraceOnLab/ConsciousnessDynamics — MIT license, Zenodo DOI forthcoming). All parameters derived from single sigmoid; no free fitting. Full reproducibility notebook included.
